          "explanation": "Rand saw lobbying as a symptom, not the disease. As long as government can hand out subsidies, tariffs, licenses and contracts, businesses will compete for them -- and honest firms must join in self-defense. Disclosure rules or better politicians would only manage the symptom. Her cure was a strict separation of state and economics, which would leave pull peddlers with nothing to sell. Public choice economists share the diagnosis but usually favor more modest institutional reforms.",
