          "explanation": "Rand's title says it: the rebels were 'cashing in' on ideas their teachers had spread. If philosophy denies that reason can settle disputes, she argued, then pressure and physical force become the natural way to get what you want -- and the sit-ins were that lesson in action. Critics answer that the movement began with a genuine free-speech grievance and drew on civil rights traditions rather than academic philosophy.",
