          "explanation": "Rand judged ideas by their root moral premise. The encyclical did not call for abolishing property or endorse Marxist economics, but it did teach that property is conditional on others' needs and that rich nations owe aid to poor ones. To Rand, that is altruism -- the same ethic she thought powered socialism -- so the Church and Marxists were, at bottom, allies against capitalism. Catholic critics answer that she ignored the Church's long defense of property and its distinction between voluntary charity and state force.",
