          "title": "Recap Dashboard: Eleven Lessons",
          "content": "A quick look back at the ground covered:\n\n• **L1-L2 -- The thesis and the definition.** Capitalism is the system of individual rights where all property is privately owned; the **trader principle** means value for value, no force.\n• **L3 -- The roots of war.** Statism breeds war; free trade breeds peace.\n• **L4 -- Greenspan's essays.** Antitrust as punishment for success; gold as a shield against inflation.\n• **L5 -- The robber barons reconsidered.** Market entrepreneurs vs. subsidized ones; Hessen on child labor and the Industrial Revolution.\n• **L6 -- Patents, copyrights, airwaves.** Property in ideas; the FCC problem as a property problem.\n• **L7 -- Conservatism: an obituary.** Tradition and faith as weak defenses of freedom.\n• **L8 -- Compromise and pull.** Lobbying as a market in government favors.\n• **L9 -- The New Left.** Berkeley 1964, alienation, and the reply to Pope Paul VI.\n• **L10 -- The other free-marketeers.** Mises, Hayek, Friedman: right conclusions, wrong foundations.\n• **L11 -- The critics.** Externalities, public goods, monopoly, the mixed-economy record, Greenspan in 2008.",
