          "explanation": "Rand held that capitalism is in fact enormously productive, but insisted that prosperity is a consequence, not the justification. If you defend markets only by their output, you accept the premise that society's welfare is the standard, and any intervention promising more welfare wins the argument. That is why she said capitalism was the unknown ideal: defended as useful, never as right. She did not regard wealth as suspect -- quite the reverse.",
